/**
 * Expo config plugin: build every Expo module from source on iOS.
 *
 * WHY THIS IS A TRACKED CONFIG PLUGIN AND NOT AN `ios/` EDIT
 * ---------------------------------------------------------
 * `apps/openagents-mobile/ios/` is gitignored derived output (see `.gitignore`),
 * regenerated by `expo prebuild --clean` on every release. This exact setting was
 * previously applied by hand to `ios/Podfile.properties.json`, which fixed the
 * crash locally, then was silently erased by the next `--clean` prebuild. The
 * regression shipped as build 125 and crashed every device at launch. A config
 * plugin runs as part of prebuild itself, so the property is re-applied every
 * time `ios/` is regenerated. Do not "simplify" this back into `ios/`.
 *
 * WHAT IT FIXES
 * -------------
 * Expo SDK 57 defaults to consuming precompiled XCFrameworks
 * (`EXPO_USE_PRECOMPILED_MODULES=1`). The published precompiled artifacts are not
 * mutually ABI-consistent: the precompiled `ExpoCamera` references the two-parameter
 * protocol witness
 *
 *   (extension in ExpoModulesCore):ExpoModulesCore.AnyModule._decorateModule(
 *     object: ExpoModulesJSI.JavaScriptObject, in: ExpoModulesJSI.JavaScriptRuntime) throws -> ()
 *
 * while `ExpoModulesCore` 57.0.2 only defines the three-parameter form that gained
 * an `appContext:` argument (`ios/Core/Protocols/AnyModule.swift`). dyld cannot
 * resolve the older symbol at launch, so the app aborts before any of our code runs:
 *
 *   Termination Reason: DYLD 4 Symbol missing
 *   Symbol not found: _$s15ExpoModulesCore9AnyModulePAAE09_decorateE06object2iny0aB3JSI16JavaScriptObjectV_AG0jK7RuntimeCtKF
 *   Referenced from: .../OpenAgents.app/Frameworks/ExpoCamera.framework/ExpoCamera
 *   Expected in:     .../OpenAgents.app/Frameworks/ExpoModulesCore.framework/ExpoModulesCore
 *
 * This is not version skew — `expo`, `expo-modules-core` and `expo-camera` all
 * resolve to 57.0.2. It is precompiled-vs-source drift, and it cannot be repaired
 * locally because the mismatch is baked into the upstream binaries. Building
 * everything from source puts all modules in one compilation universe against a
 * single `ExpoModulesCore` swiftmodule, so the witness signatures agree by
 * construction.
 *
 * HOW IT TAKES EFFECT
 * -------------------
 * The stock `expo-template-bare-minimum` Podfile (>= 57.0.6, the template this app
 * prebuilds with) force-disables on this property before applying its default:
 *
 *   ENV['EXPO_USE_PRECOMPILED_MODULES'] = '0' if podfile_properties['EXPO_USE_PRECOMPILED_MODULES'] == 'false'
 *   ENV['EXPO_USE_PRECOMPILED_MODULES'] ||= '1'
 *
 * and `expo-modules-autolinking/scripts/ios/precompiled_modules.rb` treats anything
 * other than `'1'` as disabled (`return false unless ENV[ENV_VAR] == '1'`).
 *
 * The plain assignment (not `||=`) is what makes this robust: it wins even when a
 * build environment has already exported `EXPO_USE_PRECOMPILED_MODULES=1`, which
 * EAS Build does. Note that template 57.0.2 gated the default with `||=` only, where
 * an exported env var would have beaten this property — so if the template ever
 * regresses to that form, an exporting environment must also unset the variable.
 *
 * REVISIT WHEN: Expo publishes internally consistent precompiled XCFrameworks.
 * Precompiled modules are a build-time win worth re-enabling, but only alongside a
 * symbol check on the archived `ExpoCamera`/`ExpoModulesCore` binaries — never on
 * the assumption that a version bump fixed it.
 */

const { withPodfileProperties } = require("expo/config-plugins")

const PODFILE_PROPERTY = "EXPO_USE_PRECOMPILED_MODULES"

module.exports = function withSourceBuiltExpoModules(config) {
  return withPodfileProperties(config, (podfileConfig) => {
    podfileConfig.modResults[PODFILE_PROPERTY] = "false"
    return podfileConfig
  })
}
